---
// P1 Home (doc 06 P1, CMF C1 → C14). Section order is fixed by the spec; rhythm between light, Airy Blue,
// Ice Cyan, Klein and Deep Ink bands is set with the page-local <Tone> wrapper (never two dark bands in a row).
// WP30c (owner direction 2026-10-14, "less is more"): the page is the hook for an intro call. Every band keeps its CMF place but states its point once:
// no methodology asides, no repeated explanations, no stat shown twice, FAQ answers of one to three sentences.
// WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15): Home carries the persuasion bands (Cost of Waiting, Imagine, Compare); the audience pages no longer repeat them and go straight from their own proof to their offer. So Home routes readers to
// their audience page sooner (the role router sits directly after the Results carousel) and spends fewer words on those bands: the Cost of Waiting band ends with its two cards (no closing value-proposition line) and
// the Track Record band opens with its heading (no empathy line before it). "What a Supported Youth Cohort Includes" stays: the FAQ band below it does not ask the cost question (Q8) that lists a cohort's inclusions.
// WP48 (cycle-23 review): "Evidence You Can Check" is gone (its paid-work pathways table and its 72.3% line repeated survey detail the hero strip and the carousel already carry; both stay on the Impact Survey 2026 page); its two evidence links
// close the "Proof in Practice" link row. The Low Risk band ("Start with a Multi-Cohort Pilot, Then Decide on Evidence") is gone from Home too (the audience pages keep theirs); its one line leads the closing call to action.
// WP51 (cycle-26 reviews): the comparison is headed "How CodersTrust Compares with Self-Paced Courses" (the table compares CodersTrust with one other approach), and its Outcome Tracking row carries the scope qualifier ("as agreed in the program scope");
// the positioning statement's reports are scoped the same way (POSITIONING.home); the first Imagine card is a scene ("A young woman invoices her first foreign client from her own laptop."), not "You hear from ..."; the WSDFM card of "Proof in Practice"
// shows its delivery context in place of the figure the fourth carousel slide already states (caseStudyItems).
// WP52 (cycle-27 reviews): the hero's value proposition begins "We help ..."; the carousel's government slide, speed slide and program-results slide changed (src/data/heroSlides.ts); the Results You Can Check card promises
// "Monthly reports show progress toward paid work, as agreed in the program scope."; the recognition band's AWS item has a line under its title (HomeRecognition).
// WP53 (owner decision 2026-10-16, "Trim it"): the carousel is four slides (the randomized trial, the government contracts and the National University, the Impact Survey 2026, the results by program); the reach slide and the programs slide are gone, and the two survey
// slides are one (src/data/heroSlides.ts). The band is headed "Results" and has no framing sentence: "Results and Programs" and "Evidence first, then our programs." described a programs slide that no longer exists.
// WP54 (cycle-28 reviews): the survey slide of the carousel shows its income figure directly under the heading, then the timing sentence, which now leads with its base ("Of the 170 surveyed completers who first earned during or after training, 58.8% had
// started earning by six months after finishing the course."; src/data/heroSlides.ts); the first Imagine card is "A young woman in your cohort invoices her first foreign client from her own laptop." (GLM L2: the other two cards speak to the reader's own
// program; the first read as a scene about someone else); the work-entry plan is "agreed before enrollment" (Claude S25: "approved" left open who approves).
// WP62 (cycle-34 reviews): the first slide's heading ends "per Month"; the hero's reach card no longer says "since 2014" twice (src/data/heroSlides.ts); the recognition band's press line is one pointer sentence to Recognition and Media (AsCoveredBy); the
// "Proof in Practice" link reads "See All Case Studies" (it said "Five", beside a carousel slide that says four delivered programs carry results); the "Where They Work" card says "for 12 months" (HomeMechanism).
// WP64 (cycle-36 reviews): the carousel's government slide is headed "Six Government Contracts and a National University Partnership", its program-results slide leads "Results from the records of four programs." and its trial slide says "about $27 more a month" (src/data/heroSlides.ts);
// the second Cost of Waiting card names the World Bank and the year, not the economist: "A 2017 World Bank review of nine randomized vocational-training trials found only three with significant employment impacts." (RC-06, source MCKENZIE17 unchanged).
import LandingLayout from '../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroSlider from '../components/sections/HeroSlider.astro';
import HomeHero from '../components/pages/home/HomeHero.astro';
import HomeRecognition from '../components/pages/home/HomeRecognition.astro';
import LearnerJourneys from '../components/pages/home/LearnerJourneys.astro';
import DefinitionBand from '../components/sections/DefinitionBand.astro';
import ProblemBand from '../components/sections/ProblemBand.astro';
import FutureBand from '../components/sections/FutureBand.astro';
import CaseStudyCarousel from '../components/sections/CaseStudyCarousel.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import FAQBand from '../components/sections/FAQBand.astro';
import ComparisonBand from '../components/sections/ComparisonBand.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
import WorldStrip from '../components/ui/WorldStrip.astro';
import Tone from '../components/pages/home/Tone.astro';
import HomeRouter from '../components/pages/home/HomeRouter.astro';
import HomeCost from '../components/pages/home/HomeCost.astro';
import HomeGuide from '../components/pages/home/HomeGuide.astro';
import HomeMechanism from '../components/pages/home/HomeMechanism.astro';
import Icon from '../components/system/Icon.astro';
import HomeOffer from '../components/pages/home/HomeOffer.astro';
import ConversionNextSteps from '../components/pages/home/ConversionNextSteps.astro';
import { caseStudyItems } from '../components/pages/home/caseStudies';
import { futurePhotos } from '../data/photos';
import { WORLD_STRIP } from '../data/globalStrip';
import { HOME_SLIDES } from '../data/heroSlides';
import GainsPains from '../components/pages/partners/GainsPains.astro';
import { C14, FUNDER_PAINS, HOME_META, MICRO_COMMITMENT, NEXT_STEPS_TITLE, POSITIONING, PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE, READ_THE_EVIDENCE, painForList, painForRow } from '../data/copy';
import { fact } from '../data/facts';
import { CLAIM_PX06, CLAIM_RC06, freelancePostingsFinding } from '../components/sections/copyText';
import { cta } from '../lib/mailto';
import { linkAttrs } from '../lib/url';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../lib/faq';
import { webPage } from '../lib/schema';

const discovery = cta('discovery');
const caseStudies = linkAttrs('/impact/case-studies/');
// The evidence links of the former "Evidence You Can Check" band (WP48): they close the "Proof in Practice" link row.
const trialResults = linkAttrs('/impact/independent-evaluation/');
const surveyResults = linkAttrs('/impact/outcomes-2026/');
// Q2 (national scale), Q7 (speed) and Q8 (cost) are not asked here: the offer band states the scale and the pricing, and the call to action states the timing, each once (WP17).
// WP30c: three questions, the ones a funder decides on (the country, the trial's scope, the proof); the AI question is answered by the cost-of-waiting band and the curriculum row.
// WP50 (cycle-25 review): the proof question is Home's own two-sentence variant (Q3-home), not the shared Q3, which reads as a governance answer and stays in the bank and on the audience pages that print it.
const FAQ_IDS = ['Q1', 'Q15', 'Q3-home'];
const jsonLd = [webPage({ path: '/', name: HOME_META.title, description: HOME_META.description }), faqJsonLd('home', '/', FAQ_IDS)];
// The other two funder routes sit beside the single discovery button as text links (PRD: one primary button per view).
const briefing = cta('briefing');
const introduction = cta('investor');

// C2 BLUF (WP30c): the 62 million and 19M+ figures are the two cards under it, so the sentence does not state them a second time. WP47 (cycle-22 review): two sentences, one claim each (it was one sentence joining the two with "and").
// WP50 (cycle-25 review): the second sentence speaks to the reader's own budget (it was "Training budgets rarely show who starts earning."), and the band's H2 is "Education Alone Is Not Leading to Jobs" (it was "Education Is Not Turning into Jobs").
// The closing steps band is headed NEXT_STEPS_TITLE, "What Happens Next", as on every other page with that band (it was "What Happens After You Contact Us").
const problemBluf = 'Millions of educated young people are out of work and out of training. Your training budget needs to show who starts earning.';

// C8: the three ranked pains (FUNDER_PAINS) and one C8 card for each, in that order. Numbers inside the cards come from the register.
// WP30c: only the three rows that answer a ranked pain stay; the accessible readiness assessment, the 100 training hours and the exam preparation are stated in the program options and the comparison.
// WP38 (cycle-15 review): on Home the rows are three short cards (IncludesBand), not the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix of FeaturesTable (WP39: the audience and program pages use IncludesBand too). Each card keeps its pain's id (`data-relieves`, held by
// check:facts) and its register facts (`data-fact`); every clause rests on the register: PD-01 (100 hours, three months of milestone-based mentoring, placement support alongside), PD-19 (work-entry plan agreed before
// enrollment), PD-08 and PD-09 (monthly reports, follow-up surveys, documentary evidence where available), PD-10 and PD-02 (tracks set from employer demand, AI-ready curriculum). The curriculum line keeps "designed to" (the register states the
// track menu is set from employer demand, not that the curriculum follows every change), as YouthWIDE and Investors say it. WP49 (cycle-24 review, three reviewers): it no longer says "An AI-ready curriculum is ..." ("AI-ready" is a positioning term that
// Employers and JobReady@Work explain, not Home): "A curriculum designed to follow the skills employers ask for as entry-level tasks change."
const hours = fact('PD-01').stat?.value;
// The comparison's "Independent Evidence" cell on Home (WP31): the trial in one clause, the program's length read from RC-07 (not retyped).
const trialHours = /was (\d+) hours/.exec(fact('RC-07').text)?.[1];
if (!trialHours) throw new Error('Home: RC-07 no longer reads "... was N hours"');
// WP42 (cycle-19 review): a fragment with no trailing period, like every other cell of the table (ComparisonBand).
const independentEvidence = `One randomized trial of CodersTrust’s WSDFM program (${trialHours} hours, women in Dhaka); independent evaluation of your cohort welcome`;
const includes = [
  {
    painId: painForRow(FUNDER_PAINS, 'P1').painId,
    icon: 'route',
    // WP23, item 5: placement support, not matching, toward local, remote and global work.
    title: 'Training, Mentoring and Placement Support',
    text: `${hours} training hours per certification, followed by three months of milestone-based mentoring and placement support, as agreed in the program scope. Each track’s work-entry plan is agreed before enrollment.`,
    facts: ['PD-15', 'PD-01', 'PD-19'],
  },
  {
    painId: painForRow(FUNDER_PAINS, 'P2').painId,
    icon: 'clipboard-check',
    // WP28: scoped like the FAQ and the comparison ("as agreed in the program scope"), not an unscoped inclusion. WP45 (cycle-21 review): one line. The follow-up surveys and the documentary evidence are in the FAQ ("How Do You Prove Outcomes?")
    // and on the evidence pages, so the card states the monthly reports alone (PD-08), as the positioning statement and the comparison table do.
    // WP52 (cycle-27 review, Grok M3): "Monthly reports will show ..." (it said "show", which states the reports as an existing standard; elsewhere the same promise is planned for every cohort).
    // WP58 (cycle-30 review, Claude S10): "Progress You Can Check" (it was "Results You Can Check": the card promises monthly reports, a reporting plan, not results).
    title: 'Progress You Can Check',
    text: 'Monthly reports show progress toward paid work, as agreed in the program scope.',
    facts: ['PD-08'],
  },
  {
    painId: painForRow(FUNDER_PAINS, 'P3').painId,
    icon: 'briefcase',
    title: 'Tracks Chosen from Employer Demand',
    text: 'A curriculum designed to follow the skills employers ask for as entry-level tasks change.',
    facts: ['PD-02', 'PD-10'],
  },
];
---

<LandingLayout title={HOME_META.title} titleSuffix={false} description={HOME_META.description} jsonLd={jsonLd} stickyCta={{ label: discovery.label, href: discovery.href }}>
  <Tone cmf="C1"><HomeHero id="hero" /></Tone>
  <!-- WP19, item 6: "What Is CodersTrust?" sits directly under the hero, before the Results carousel. -->
  <Tone cmf="GEO"><DefinitionBand id="definition" /></Tone>
  <Tone cmf="RESULTS">
    <HeroSlider id="results" label="Results" heading="Results" slides={HOME_SLIDES} />
  </Tone>

  <!-- WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15): the site is the hook for an introductory call, so the role router sits directly after the Results carousel, where a reader can reach their audience page sooner (it was the band before the
       closing call to action; WP23). One router on the page; the hero's own audience links stay. Its own light ground (airy) keeps the rhythm between the carousel above and the white problem band below. -->
  <Tone cmf="ROUTER"><HomeRouter id="router" /></Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C2">
    <ProblemBand id="problem" title="Education Alone Is Not Leading to Jobs" bluf={problemBluf} factIds={['PX-01', 'PX-02']}>
      <GainsPains slot="lead" painsHeading="What Gets in the Way" pains={FUNDER_PAINS.map(painForList)} />
    </ProblemBand>
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C3">
    <HomeCost
      id="cost"
      title="Training and Evidence Fall Behind While You Wait"
      blocks={[
        // WP38 (cycle-15 review): the card states the first finding of PX-06 (the 21% on one platform), not both findings of the study in one sentence; PX-06 stays the fact the line rests on.
        { icon: 'cpu', claim: CLAIM_PX06, factId: 'PX-06', text: freelancePostingsFinding(), implication: 'Training has to follow current employer demand, not last year’s job market.' },
        { icon: 'trending-down', claim: CLAIM_RC06, factId: 'RC-06', implication: 'Without outcome tracking, funders cannot tell which programs reach earnings.' },
      ]}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- WP19, item 6 of the home order: credibility (the guide) comes before the vision (the next 12 months). Home only. -->
  <Tone cmf="C5" tone="white"><HomeGuide id="guide" /></Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C4" tone="airy">
    <FutureBand
      photos={futurePhotos('home')}
      id="future"
      title="Imagine the Next 12 Months"
      lead="Three illustrative scenarios, not case studies."
      vignettes={[
        { kind: 'Functional', title: 'A First Foreign Client, Billed from Home', text: 'A young woman in your cohort invoices her first foreign client from her own laptop.' },
        { kind: 'Emotional', title: 'First Earnings, Not Just Certificates', text: 'You review monthly reports, as agreed in the program scope, showing who is earning, not only who completed.' },
        // WP48 (cycle-23 review, three reviewers): not "AI-Ready Talent" ("AI-ready" is a positioning term explained on Employers and JobReady@Work, which Home does not carry); the scenario says what the reader sees.
        { kind: 'Social', title: 'Employers Hiring from Your Cohort', text: 'You see employers hire completers whose skills match current employer demand.' },
      ]}
    />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C6"><HomeMechanism id="mechanism" title="One Path from Learning to Earning" tone="white" positioning={POSITIONING.home} link={{ label: 'How Our Model Works', href: '/our-model/' }} /></Tone>

  <!-- WP19, item 8: the "At a Glance" band is gone. WP25h: the band no longer retells the trial and the survey (the carousel states them). WP35 (cycle-12 review): nor the trial at all (the hero card and the first slide state it); the band kept the paid-work pathways
       beside the 72.3% no-prior-income result (34 of 47). WP48 (cycle-23 review): both are gone from Home (the hero's survey card and the carousel carry the survey; the Impact Survey 2026 page keeps the table and the 72.3%), which left "Evidence You Can Check" with its two
       links alone, so the band is gone and its two links sit in the link row of "Proof in Practice" below (the C7 proof position). -->
  <Tone cmf="C7" join>
    <!-- WP37 (cycle-14 review): the program-results slide of the carousel (slide 4) states the Kosovo and Her Power figures, so those two cards show delivery context instead (caseStudyItems). WP51 (cycle-26 review): the same slide states the WSDFM figure too
         (WP50), so all three cards show delivery context and none repeats a figure. -->
    <CaseStudyCarousel id="cases" eyebrow="Case Studies" title="Proof in Practice" items={caseStudyItems}>
      <a slot="more" class="link" href={caseStudies.href}>See All Case Studies<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a>
      <a slot="more" class="link" href={trialResults.href}>Read the Trial Results<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a>
      <a slot="more" class="link" href={surveyResults.href}>Impact Survey 2026<Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} /></a>
    </CaseStudyCarousel>
    <!-- WP25h (benchmark review): three registered learner stories, one from each program above, replace the single Her Power learner voice (Maria Dewan is one of the three). -->
    <LearnerJourneys id="journeys" tone="airy" />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="RECOGNITION"><HomeRecognition id="recognition" /></Tone>

  <!-- WP55 (owner decisions 2026-10-17/18, global positioning): CodersTrust is a New York organization with work in 16 countries and territories, so Home carries one small strip of where, in order, ending on Bangladesh (where most delivery has been). Its own
       light ground (ice) keeps the rhythm between the white recognition band above and the airy band below. -->
  <Tone cmf="GLOBAL" tone="ice">
    <Section tone="ice" aria-labelledby="world-h"><WorldStrip tiles={WORLD_STRIP} level={2} id="world" /></Section>
  </Tone>

  <!-- WP38: three short cards (IncludesBand) in place of the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix; one band, so no `join` (it had left this band without bottom padding). -->
  <Tone cmf="C8" tone="airy">
    <IncludesBand id="features" tone="airy" title="What a Supported Youth Cohort Includes" cards={includes} />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C9" tone="white">
    <FAQBand id="faq" audience="home" ids={FAQ_IDS} title="Questions Partners Ask" allLink={{ label: 'Find the Answers for Your Route', href: '/partner-with-us/#audiences' }} />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C10" tone="ice"><ComparisonBand id="compare" title="How CodersTrust Compares with Self-Paced Courses" lead="What each approach typically includes." withoutDoingNothing onlyRows={['Mentoring', 'Work Entry', 'Outcome Tracking', 'Independent Evidence']} dropColumns={['Conventional Skills Programs', 'Freelance Marketplaces Alone']} ownCells={{ 'Independent Evidence': independentEvidence }} /></Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C11"><HomeOffer id="offer" lead={PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE} /></Tone>

  <!-- C12 (Low Risk) is left to the audience pages since WP48 (cycle-23 review): Home's four cards (pilot, scorecard thresholds, expansion review, independent evaluation) repeated points made in "Choose Where to Start", the FAQ and the comparison, so
       the one line that survives is the closing band's lead, directly above the call to action. -->

  <!-- WP45 (cycle-21 review): the band has no "Planning a Grant-Funded Cohort?" block: it assumed grant funding for every audience that reaches the page (ministries, employers, impact investors), and the grant timeline is in the C14 steps below. -->
  <Tone cmf="C13">
    <CTABand
      id="cta"
      tone="klein"
      heading="Let’s Design Your First Cohort"
      text="Start with a multi-cohort pilot, agree the scorecard up front, and decide on expansion from the evidence."
      cta={{ label: discovery.label, href: discovery.href }}
      secondary={{ label: READ_THE_EVIDENCE, href: '/impact/' }}
      routes={[
        { audience: 'Governments', label: briefing.label, href: briefing.href },
        { audience: 'Impact investors', label: introduction.label, href: introduction.href },
      ]}
      micro={MICRO_COMMITMENT}
    />
  </Tone>

  <Tone cmf="C14">
    <!-- The 6–8 week start is stated in the "First cohort" step only (doc 04 §4, one statement per fact; WP45 removed the C13 plan line that stated it too): no PD-04 timing line, no reminder. The micro-commitment is stated once, in C13. -->
    <!-- WP28: the week-by-week steps are labelled "For Grant-Funded Pilots" (WP46, cycle-22 review: it read "Cohorts"; the hub's and Development Partners' timing is for grant-funded pilots), and one line names the audiences that get a route-specific next step. WP30c: the four steps were their headings alone (each names its week; the sentences under them restated the headings); WP49 (cycle-24 review): each step has its one-line description again, the hub's (grantStartSteps, ConversionNextSteps' default), because the hub and the audience pages describe theirs. -->
    <ConversionNextSteps
      id="next-steps"
      eyebrow="Target Timing for Grant-Funded Pilots"
      title={NEXT_STEPS_TITLE}
      timing={false}
      firstAction={C14.firstActionLabeled}
      otherRoutes={{
        audiences: [
          { label: 'Ministries', href: '/partner-with-us/governments/' },
          { label: 'employers', href: '/partner-with-us/employers/' },
          { label: 'impact investors', href: '/partner-with-us/investors/' },
        ],
        text: 'get a route-specific next step.',
      }}
    />
  </Tone>

  <!-- WP31 (cycle-8 review): the "Latest News" band (Bangladesh posts after the final call to action) is gone, so the page ends on its next steps. The News menu item stays. -->
</LandingLayout>

